# ------------------------------------------------- paging

[break] the-list-cursor-is-ignored
rule: A page of `session/list` holds what comes after the last summary of the page before, in the list's order.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/core.rs
in: handle
find: .is_none_or(|after| after.is_before(summary))
replace: .is_none_or(|after| after.is_before(summary) || !after.session.as_str().is_empty())
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it turns::the_list_is_paged_by_the_last_summary_given_so_nothing_moves_between_pages

[break] the-lists-tie-is-not-broken-by-the-id
rule: Two sessions used at the same moment are told apart by their ids, so a page boundary between them skips neither.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/core.rs
in: ListCursor::is_before
find: time < self.updated_at || (time == self.updated_at && summary.session_id < self.session)
replace: time < self.updated_at
caught-by:
    cortex-core core::tests::a_list_cursor_gives_what_comes_after_it_ties_broken_by_the_id

[break] the-list-says-there-is-no-more
rule: A page that has sessions after it gives the cursor to them.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/core.rs
in: handle
find: sessions.iter().any(|summary| at.is_before(summary))
replace: sessions.iter().any(|summary| at.is_before(summary) && summary.turns == u64::MAX)
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it turns::the_list_is_paged_by_the_last_summary_given_so_nothing_moves_between_pages
